  </div>
          <p>The <span class=3D"ocpUserInput">sfc /scannow</span> command w=
ill scan all protected system files and replace corrupted files with a cach=
ed copy.&nbsp; The scan results will be shown after this process is finishe=
d. You may receive one of the following messages:</p>
          <table aria-label=3D"" class=3D"banded flipColors">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>
                  <p>
                    <b class=3D"ocpLegacyBold">Scan result message</b>
                  </p>
                </th>
                <th>
                  <p>
                    <b class=3D"ocpLegacyBold">Corresponding action</b>
                  </p>
                </th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <p>Windows Resource Protection did not find any integrity=
 violations.</p>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <p>You do not have any missing or corrupted system files.=
</p>
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <p>Windows Resource Protection could not perform the requ=
ested operation.</p>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <p>To resolve this problem, perform the System File Check=
er scan <a href=3D"https://support.microsoft.com/windows/windows-startup-se=
ttings-1af6ec8c-4d4a-4b23-adb7-e76eef0b847f" target=3D"_blank" class=3D"ocp=
ExternalLink" data-bi-type=3D"anchor">in safe mode</a>.</p>
                  <p>Make sure that the <b class=3D"ocpUI">PendingDeletes</=
b> and <b class=3D"ocpUI">PendingRenames</b> folders exist under <b class=
=3D"ocpUI">%WinDir%\WinSxS\Temp</b>.</p>
                  <p>The %WinDir% placeholder represents the Windows operat=
ing system folder, such as, C:\Windows.</p>
                </td>
              </tr>
